<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<component type="desktop">
  <id>cc.etke.komai</id>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">@KOMAI_DESKTOP_ID@.desktop</launchable>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <developer id="cc.etke">
    <name>Komai</name>
  </developer>
  <name>Komai</name>
  <summary>A Matrix chat app you can get to love</summary>
  <description>
    <p>Komai is a desktop-first Matrix chat application built with Rust, C++ and QML. It is optimized for large screens, with comfortably readable text, generous hit targets, and a user interface that treats both newcomers and power users as capable adults: neither dumbed down nor buried in complexity.</p>
    <p>Komai began as a usability-focused fork of nheko, but has since been heavily rebuilt around the Rust matrix-sdk runtime and a growing Rust core.</p>
    <p>Features include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Matrix messaging with end-to-end encryption support</li>
      <li>Voice and video calls</li>
      <li>File, image, audio and custom-emoji messages, with a built-in media viewer including gallery navigation and in-app video playback</li>
      <li>Smarter emoji search using localized Unicode CLDR keywords</li>
      <li>Replies, threads, and message forwarding</li>
      <li>Multi-account support via dedicated application profiles</li>
      <li>10+ built-in themes meeting WCAG AA contrast guidelines, plus user-themable support</li>
      <li>30+ languages</li>
      <li>Browser-style room tabs with pinning, for juggling multiple conversations</li>
      <li>Keyboard shortcuts for the main chat workflow, with human- and Vim-style bindings</li>
      <li>First-class Matrix room search and room-size filtering</li>
      <li>Selection mode for bulk actions like forwarding and moderation</li>
      <li>Local automation via Model Context Protocol (MCP), CLI commands, and D-Bus</li>
      <li>Native and lightweight — no Electron</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Komai is fully Free Software (GPL-3.0-or-later), with no CLA and no contributor gatekeeping.</p>
  </description>
